    "evidence_text": "This paper reviews stateof-the-art approaches and systems for word segmentation in Vietnamese.\n\nThis paper aims reviewing state-of-the-art word segmentation approaches and systems applying for Vietnamese.\n\nSection V mainly addresses two existing toolkits, vnTokenizer and JVnSegmenter, for Vietnamese word segmentation.\n\nThere are three methods to identify morphemes in Vietnamese text  .\n\nBUILDING MODEL METHODS\tThere are several studies for Vietnamese Word Segmentation during last decade.\n\nMany researchers applied Hidden Markov model to solve Vietnamese word segmentation such as in  ,  and so on.\n\nN-gram language modeling applied to estimate probabilities for each word segmentation solution  .\n\nMaximum Entropy (ME)\tMaximum Entropy theory is applied to solve Vietnamese word segmentation  ,  ,  .\n\nSo, they use the context around of the word needed to be segmented.\n\nEVALUATION AND RESULTS\tThis research gathers the results of Vietnamese word segmentation of several methods into one table as show in Table II.\n\nThis study also evaluates the Vietnamese word segmentation based on existing toolkits using the same annotated Vietnamese word segmentation corpus.\n\nCONCLUSIONS AND FUTURE WORKS\tThis study reviewed state-of-the-art approaches and systems of Vietnamese word segmentation.\n\nThe review pointed out common features and methods used in Vietnamese word segmentation studies.",
